WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们现在是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
我们正在为你们制作《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:25.280
Hello.
你好。

9
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.340
Hi there.
嗨。

10
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.780
Are you excited to go to a super cringy fundraiser today?
你期待今天去参加那个超级尴尬的筹款活动吗？

11
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:30.940
I am.
我很期待。

12
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.380
I'm going to get my best little hairdo going.
我要把我的发型弄得漂漂亮亮的。

13
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.400
Oh, I have fan questions about your hairdo, Angela.
噢，安吉拉，粉丝们对你的发型有疑问。

14
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.380
Well, let's save it.
好吧，我们先留着以后再说。

15
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:38.840
Okay.
好的。

16
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.440
We have a lot to discuss.
我们有很多要讨论的。

17
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.340
Today is Season 8, Episode 22.
今天是第八季第22集。

18
00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:46.780
It was written by Owen Ellickson and directed by Dave Rogers.
由欧文·埃利克森编剧，戴夫·罗杰斯执导。

19
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.280
Here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

20
00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:54.960
The Dunder Mifflin Group is concerned when newly unemployed Andy displays some questionable behavior,
邓德·米夫林公司的人对刚失业的安迪表现出的可疑行为感到担忧，

21
00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:01.560
both in the Dunder Mifflin parking lot and later at an animal welfare fundraiser hosted by the senator.
无论是在邓德·米夫林的停车场，还是后来在参议员举办的动物福利筹款活动上。

22
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:02.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

23
00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:14.720
Also at the fundraiser, Oscar becomes convinced that the senator is hitting on him, Dwight misunderstands the rules of a silent auction, and Andy adopts 12 senior dogs.
同样在筹款活动上，奥斯卡开始确信参议员在勾引他，德怀特误解了无声拍卖的规则，而安迪领养了12只老年犬。

24
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.380
Andy, Andy, Andy.
安迪，安迪，安迪。

25
00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:29.600
As someone who has worked in animal rescue, I can tell you that one needy animal, one animal that needs medications and ointments and salves is enough.
作为一个从事过动物救援工作的人，我可以告诉你，照顾一只需要药物、药膏和软膏的弱势动物就已经够累了。

26
00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:30.540
You don't need 12.
你根本不需要12只。

27
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.120
That's a hard job.
那是一项艰巨的工作。

28
00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.940
I mean, Aaron says this is my life now.
我是说，亚伦说这就是我现在的全部生活了。

29
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:35.540
I know.
我知道。

30
00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:37.900
All right.
好吧。

31
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.300
Fast fact number one.
速览事实第一条。

32
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.720
Angela, you know how much I love when you do fast fact number three.
安吉拉，你知道我有多喜欢你讲速览事实第三条。

33
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.980
And today you are doing fast fact number one.
今天轮到你讲速览事实第一条了。

34
00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:47.860
I am.
没错。

35
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:48.220
Okay.
好的。

36
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.740
For those of you guys that have the DVD box set, we are now on disc five.
对于那些拥有DVD套装的朋友，我们现在讲到第五张碟了。

37
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.480
And let me tell you, there's some special features.
我得告诉你们，里面有一些特别花絮。

38
00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.080
First of all, fundraiser has an extended producer's cut.
首先，《筹款活动》有一集加长制片人剪辑版。

39
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:05.880
But there is also, under the bonus section, a 19-minute blooper reel.
但在奖励部分，还有一个19分钟的NG花絮集锦。

40
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.260
I watched the whole 19 minutes.
我把这19分钟全看完了。

41
00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.820
It was a joy.
真是种享受。

42
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.200
I mean, if you need a laugh, watch a 19-minute blooper reel.
我是说，如果你想笑一笑，就去看那19分钟的NG花絮。

43
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.520
I love our blooper reels.
我爱我们的NG花絮。

44
00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.560
I do, too.
我也是。

45
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.520
They're my favorite thing.
它们是我的最爱。

46
00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:19.160
Me, too.
我也是。

47
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.160
They just take me back right away.
它们能瞬间把我带回过去。

48
00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.540
We talk about this all the time, that we went to work and tried not to laugh all day.
我们经常说，我们去上班时整天都在努力憋笑。

49
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:26.980
What a blessing.
真是种福气。

50
00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:27.540
Yes.
是的。

51
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.380
Okay.
好的。

52
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:32.040
It also has the webisode series, The Girl Next Door.
里面还收录了网络剧集《隔壁女孩》。

53
00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:38.180
And apparently, NBC was hosting Super Bowl XLVI.
显然，当时NBC主办了第四十六届超级碗。

54
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:38.980
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

55
00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:43.180
And we did a bunch of promos, like a lot.
我们拍了很多宣传片，真的非常多。

56
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.960
And they're all on there.
它们全都收录在里面了。

57
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.900
To remind you guys, Super Bowl XLVI was the New York Jets versus New England Patriots.
提醒一下大家，第四十六届超级碗是纽约喷气机队对阵新英格兰爱国者队。

58
00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.080
The Jets won 21 to 17.
喷气机队以21比17获胜。

59
00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.720
Kelly Clarkson sang the national anthem.
凯莉·克拉克森演唱了国歌。

60
00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.080
And Madonna was the big halftime show.
麦当娜担任了中场秀的重磅嘉宾。

61
00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.960
Well, I remember these promos.
嗯，我记得这些宣传片。

62
00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.200
We did one promo with all of the NBC shows.
我们拍过一支汇集了所有NBC节目的宣传片。

63
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.760
And it was based on a musical number from How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying.
它是基于音乐剧《平步青云》里的一段音乐改编的。

64
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.060
And it kicked off with 30 Rock.
开头是《我为喜剧狂》。

65
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.640
And then our cast sang part of it.
然后我们的演员也唱了一部分。

66
00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.080
It was...
那是……

67
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.760
Do, do, do, do, do, do, do, do.
嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟。

68
00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:17.940
Do, do.
嘟，嘟。

69
00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.080
What's this song?
这是什么歌？

70
00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.460
Do, do, do, do, do, do.
嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟，嘟。

71
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.260
Of men.
男人们。

72
00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:22.900
Yes.
是的。

73
00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:23.360
Yes.
没错。

74
00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:24.820
And da, da, da, da, da.
还有哒，哒，哒，哒，哒。

75
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:26.800
Da, da, da, da, da, da, da.
哒，哒，哒，哒，哒，哒，哒。

76
00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:27.920
You know I'm horrible at this, right?
你知道我不擅长这个，对吧？

77
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:33.180
Like, if I had to go on a game show and really lose badly, it would be like, guess the tune.
如果我非得去参加那种会输得很惨的游戏节目，那肯定就是猜曲名之类的。

78
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:33.760
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

79
00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:34.540
Because I'm just like...
因为我只会……

80
00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.420
But I don't know.
但我不知道。

81
00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.000
I can't...
我没法……

82
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.160
In the company of men.
在男人的陪伴下。

83
00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:37.540
Yes.
是的。

84
00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:37.960
Maybe?
也许吧？

85
00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.600
I'm going to say yes to everything.
我什么都说好。

86
00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:40.060
Okay.
好吧。

87
00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:41.960
But it was huge.
但那支宣传片规模很大。

88
00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.260
It was choreographed and we're lip syncing and it's so charming.
它有专门的编舞，我们是在假唱，看起来非常迷人。

89
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.620
And it was big.
而且规模宏大。

90
00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:52.580
The full promo with all of the NBC people doing it was like, oh my gosh, six minutes?
那支由所有NBC成员参与的完整宣传片，天哪，有六分钟长吧？

91
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.260
It was long.
它很长。

92
00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:54.120
It was very long.
非常长。

93
00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:55.400
It's so fun to watch.
看起来特别有趣。

94
00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.280
It is not on this DVD.
它没收录在这张DVD里。

95
00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.380
Oh, never mind everyone.
噢，大家别管了。

96
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.680
Google it.
去谷歌搜一下吧。

97
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:01.980
It is out there.
网上有的。

98
00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.420
Here are the Super Bowl promos on this DVD.
这张DVD里收录的是这些超级碗宣传片。

99
00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:09.720
First, there's a commercial where Kevin is really excited about the Super Bowl commercials.
首先是一个广告，凯文对超级碗的广告感到非常兴奋。

100
00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.780
And then Robert California pitches his idea for the perfect Super Bowl commercial.
然后是罗伯特·加利福尼亚推销他关于完美超级碗广告的点子。

101
00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.620
I'm scared.
我很害怕。

102
00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:17.700
Yeah, you should be.
没错，你是该害怕。

103
00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.180
It would feature a woman in her late 60s.
主角是一位六十多岁的女性。

104
00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:26.280
And everywhere she goes, men fall to their knees, crippled with luSt.
无论她走到哪里，男人们都会因强烈的欲望而跪倒在地，动弹不得。

105
00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:31.780
She sees the camera while grocery shopping and drops her basket and looks right at the camera
她在买菜时看到了摄像机，于是放下篮子，直视镜头，

106
00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:34.240
and says, this was all part of your plan.
然后说，这一切都是你的计划。

107
00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.240
Wasn't it, Robert?
不是吗，罗伯特？

108
00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.820
And then Kevin says, wait, how can you do that?
然后凯文说，等等，你怎么能做到那样？

109
00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.000
How can you make the commercial different for every single person?
你怎么能让广告对每个人来说都不一样？

110
00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.720
And Robert goes, I don't know.
罗伯特就说，我不知道。

111
00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:44.700
I don't watch television.
我不看电视。

112
00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.220
That's weird.
那真奇怪。

113
00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:46.940
I know.
我知道。

114
00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.740
This was made.
这是制作出来的。

115
00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:49.480
Yes.
是的。

116
00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:50.300
It's on the DVD.
在DVD里有。

117
00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:50.940
It's on the DVD.
在DVD里有。

118
00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:51.360
Okay.
好吧。

119
00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.280
The next promo was called Fans.
下一个宣传片叫《粉丝》。

120
00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.540
And it's Andy and Erin just saying right to camera, you guys are going to the Super Bowl.
安迪和艾琳对着镜头说，你们要去超级碗现场了。

121
00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.740
That must be so exciting.
那一定很令人兴奋。

122
00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:00.940
And they're very cute and charming.
他们看起来非常可爱迷人。

123
00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.940
Then there's one called Museums, and it's John and Rain as themselves.
然后还有一个叫《博物馆》，是约翰和雷恩以他们本人的身份出镜。

124
00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.140
But they're dressed in character, and they're on set.
但他们穿着角色的服装，在片场里。

125
00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.020
And Rain is telling everyone what museums they should go to instead of going to the game,
雷恩在告诉大家应该去哪些博物馆，而不是去看比赛，

126
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.260
kind of like in hopes to get their tickets.
大概是希望能拿到他们的票。

127
00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:16.240
Got it.
明白了。

128
00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.340
It was very cute.
非常可爱。

129
00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:22.520
There's one called Post Game, where Ed is dressed as Andy, and he's sitting in the manager's office.
有一个叫《赛后》，艾德穿着安迪的衣服，坐在经理办公室里。

130
00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:28.060
And he's encouraging everyone to stick around after the Super Bowl to watch the post game celebration.
他鼓励大家在超级碗结束后留下来观看赛后庆祝活动。

131
00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:28.740
Okay.
好的。

132
00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.460
NBC really wanted people to stick around.
NBC真的很想让人留下来。

133
00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:35.320
Oh, that's why they always fight over who gets to air the Super Bowl.
哦，这就是为什么他们总是争夺超级碗的转播权。

134
00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.100
I mean, first of all, obviously, the ad revenue.
我是说，首先，显而易见，是为了广告收入。

135
00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:39.660
Right, right.
没错，没错。

136
00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:45.880
But afterwards, they would use the Super Bowl to, like, launch new shows or highlight shows that they really were excited about.
但之后，他们会利用超级碗来推出新节目，或者宣传他们非常看好的节目。

137
00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:46.300
Yeah.
是的。

138
00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.840
Stick around after the Super Bowl.
超级碗结束后请留下来。

139
00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:48.260
Yeah.
是的。

140
00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.300
They say it all the time.
他们总是这么说。

141
00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.880
And then my favorite one was called Dip.
然后我最喜欢的一个叫《蘸酱》。

142
00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:57.400
And Kevin is going to share his perfect Super Bowl dip recipe.
凯文要分享他完美的超级碗蘸酱配方。

143
00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.140
You need to hear it.
你一定要听听。

144
00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:00.680
Brotherhood of Man.
《人类兄弟情》。

145
00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:01.320
Yes.
是的。

146
00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.500
That's the name of the song.
那是那首歌的名字。

147
00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:03.240
There you go.
这就对了。

148
00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:09.240
In honor of the Super Bowl, I have made 46-layer dip.
为了纪念超级碗，我做了46层蘸酱。

149
00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:18.320
Refried beans, ground beef, super salsa, bacon, graham cracker, bacon, seven-layer dip, but all in one layer,
油炸豆泥、碎牛肉、超级莎莎酱、培根、全麦饼干、培根、七层蘸酱，但全都在一层里，

150
00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.860
garden burger, turkey burger, beef burger, grilled cheese sandwiches.
素食汉堡、火鸡汉堡、牛肉汉堡、烤奶酪三明治。

151
00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.700
Kevin, I need that report by five.
凯文，我五点前需要那份报告。

152
00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.580
Now I have to start over, Andy.
现在我得重头开始了，安迪。

153
00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:28.560
Gosh.
天哪。

154
00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:31.360
Refried beans.
炸豆泥。

155
00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.520
Ground beef.
碎牛肉。

156
00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:33.600
Super salsa.
超级莎莎酱。

157
00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:40.300
It's working for me, but the graham cracker was—
这对我来说挺管用，但全麦饼干……

158
00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.340
That really threw you.
那真的让你困惑了。

159
00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.580
Yeah, that threw me off.
是啊，那确实让我乱了阵脚。

160
00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:48.300
There is an actual giant tub of this stuff, and he's pointing to each layer.
这玩意儿居然有一大桶，而且他还在指着每一层。

161
00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.040
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

162
00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.920
I'm going to put a picture of it in stories.
我要把它拍张照发到快拍里。

163
00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:51.540
Okay, please.
好的，拜托了。

164
00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:52.760
It looks disgusting.
看起来真恶心。

165
00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:58.340
And those are the bonus features on the last disc of season eight.
那些就是第八季最后一张光盘里的花絮内容。

166
00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.360
That was a very good report, Angela.
那份报告写得非常好，安吉拉。

167
00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.660
I enjoyed it very much.
我非常喜欢。

168
00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:02.520
Okay, well, thank you.
好的，谢谢。

169
00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.120
Let's move on to fast fact number two.
让我们进入第二个速览事实。

170
00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:09.300
One of the storylines in this week's episode was inspired by a true story.
本周剧集里的一个故事情节是受真实故事启发而来的。

171
00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:19.760
So, you know, at the charity event, they have a silent auction, but Dwight thinks this is a guess the price game and that you win the prize if you guess the correct price.
你知道，在慈善活动上，他们举行了无声拍卖，但德怀特以为这是一个猜价格游戏，只要猜中正确价格就能赢得奖品。

172
00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:20.120
Yeah.
没错。

173
00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:25.040
Well, this happened to our writer, Halstead Sullivan's sister, in real life.
嗯，这事儿在现实生活中发生在我们编剧哈尔斯特德·沙利文的姐姐身上。

174
00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.280
I cannot believe that.
我简直不敢相信。

175
00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.820
It's so crazy.
太疯狂了。

176
00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:29.520
Tell the story.
讲讲这个故事吧。

177
00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:35.620
So, he was working at the office at the time, and his sister called him on the phone and was like,
当时他正在办公室工作，他姐姐打电话给他，说：

178
00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:43.140
Halstead, I won this expensive Italian sofa at this event last night.
哈尔斯特德，我昨晚在活动上赢了一张昂贵的意大利沙发。

179
00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:48.540
It's worth $17,000, and I guessed the price exactly, and I won.
它价值17000美元，我猜的价格分毫不差，所以我赢了。

180
00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.820
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

181
00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.740
And he was like, that's amazing.
他说，那太棒了。

182
00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:52.380
Congratulations.
恭喜你。

183
00:07:53.080 --> 00:08:01.560
But then cut to a few days later, she called him to say that the charity sent her a really weird letter asking her to pay for the sofa.
但几天后，她打电话告诉他，慈善机构寄来一封很奇怪的信，要求她为那张沙发付款。

184
00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.400
And he said, fax me the letter.
他说，把信传真给我。

185
00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.340
When Halstead was retelling the story, he said, old tech alert.
哈尔斯特德重述这个故事时说，老式科技预警。

186
00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.140
Yes, she faxed me the letter from the charity.
是的，她把慈善机构的信传真给了我。

187
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.340
And he looked it over, and he had to explain to her that it was not a guess the price.
他看了一遍，不得不向她解释，那根本不是什么猜价格游戏。

188
00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:23.880
It was a silent auction, and that her bid for the sofa was $17,000, and they wanted to collect.
那是无声拍卖，她对沙发的出价是17000美元，他们是来收款的。

189
00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.480
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

190
00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.640
He said she panicked.
他说她当时惊慌失措。

191
00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:28.780
Well, yeah.
那是肯定的。

192
00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:35.480
He also said in her defense, there was an Italian man with an accent who had explained the rules.
他还说，为她辩解一下，当时有个带口音的意大利男人向她解释了规则。

193
00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:42.880
And perhaps something got lost in translation, but she called the charity.
可能是在翻译过程中出了点偏差，但她给慈善机构打了电话。

194
00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.840
She explained the mistake, and they did not make her pay $17,000.
她解释了误会，他们最终没有让她支付那17000美元。

195
00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.020
Halstead said he recognized the sofa she bid on.
哈尔斯特德说他认出了她出价的那张沙发。

196
00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.560
It was a DeSeddy sofa?
是DeSeddy沙发吗？

197
00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:56.460
DeSed?
DeSed？

198
00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.320
D-E-S-E-D-E.
D-E-S-E-D-E。

199
00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:03.720
It is an Italian sofa, which is basically the Birkin bag of sofas.
那是一款意大利沙发，基本上就是沙发界的爱马仕铂金包。

200
00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:07.120
$17,000 is actually a bargain.
17000美元其实算捡到便宜了。

201
00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.720
I can't even wrap my head around that number.
我简直无法想象那个数字。

202
00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:10.520
That's a car.
那是一辆车的价格。

203
00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:11.320
Yeah.
是啊。

204
00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:12.880
That's like you're sitting on a car.
就好像你坐在车上一样。

205
00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:22.540
Well, Halstead said he only recognized it because before they wrote on The Office, he and Warren had written for a show produced by Will Smith and Jada Pinkett Smith,
嗯，霍尔斯特德说他之所以认出来，是因为在他们写《办公室》之前，他和沃伦曾为威尔·史密斯和贾达·萍克特·史密斯制作的一档节目写过剧本，

206
00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:24.400
and they had one of these sofas.
他们当时就有这种沙发。

207
00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:24.760
Oh!
噢！

208
00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:30.240
It was written up in like, you know, one of those profiles they do of celebrity homes.
那是在那种名人住宅专题报道里写到的。

209
00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:30.580
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊，是啊。

210
00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:33.780
And I looked at the website.
我查了下网站。

211
00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:37.660
Most of these sofas go for around $40,000.
这种沙发大多要卖到4万美元左右。

212
00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.200
Wow.
哇。

213
00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:47.700
And I'm very sorry, DeSeddy or DeSed sofa company, but they are ugly.
我很抱歉，DeSeddy还是DeSed沙发公司，但它们真的很难看。

214
00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.000
I'm just going to say it.
我直说了吧。

215
00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.060
They are—
它们简直——

216
00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:54.240
Will you send me a picture of one?
你能发张照片给我看看吗？

217
00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:54.900
Yes.
可以。

218
00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:55.680
I mean—
我是说——

219
00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:56.460
Do you want to see it?
你想看吗？

220
00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:56.760
Yeah.
想。

221
00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:57.760
Are they comfortable?
它们舒服吗？

222
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.280
They can't be $40,000 comfortable.
不可能舒服到值4万美元。

223
00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:03.900
They don't—nothing is $40,000 comfortable.
它们不——没有什么东西能舒服到值4万美元。

224
00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:04.180
Nothing.
什么都没有。

225
00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:15.320
Like, if you take the most comfortable $1,500 couch, it is not—this special sofa is not 40 times more comfortable than it.
比如，如果你拿一张最舒服的1500美元的沙发来比，这种所谓的特殊沙发绝对不可能比它舒服40倍。

226
00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:15.840
You know what?
你知道吗？

227
00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:20.960
We have a couch from Ikea that Josh put together himself, and when he said, I'm going to put it together,
我们有个宜家的沙发是乔什自己组装的，当他说“我要把它装起来”的时候，

228
00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:24.660
I thought maybe it comes in four pieces you screw on the legs.
我以为可能就是四块零件，拧上腿就行了。

229
00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:25.540
You know what I mean?
你懂我的意思吧？

230
00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:25.920
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

231
00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:26.920
No, Jenna.
不，珍娜。

232
00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.900
There's a box that's just the stuffing.
有个箱子里装的全是填充物。

233
00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.880
Then you got to, like, stuff it, and you got to, like—you literally build a couch.
然后你得去填充它，你得——你简直是在造一张沙发。

234
00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:39.300
And I thought, wow, this—we're getting such a deal on this sectional.
我当时想，哇，这套组合沙发我们买得太划算了。

235
00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.200
It's because you build the whole damn thing.
原来是因为你得自己把这该死的东西全造出来。

236
00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:46.120
Yes, there's no—well, they don't charge you for any labor because you are the labor.
没错，没有——好吧，他们不收你人工费，因为你就是那个劳动力。

237
00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:47.740
It took a whole day.
花了一整天时间。

238
00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.600
But is it comfortable?
但它舒服吗？

239
00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:50.760
Yes.
舒服。

240
00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:51.260
Right.
也是。

241
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.760
Now, I just—here's the website.
现在，我只是——这是网站。

242
00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:54.660
Oh, no.
噢，不。

243
00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:55.160
Right?
对吧？

244
00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.320
This is ridiculous.
这太荒谬了。

245
00:10:56.620 --> 00:11:00.480
One of their things is that they make, like, a snake sofa.
他们其中一款产品是所谓的“蛇形沙发”。

246
00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:05.600
It doesn't look like a snake, but you can, I guess, make it into an S shape.
它看起来不像蛇，但我猜你可以把它摆成S形。

247
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.460
I'll tell you—
我跟你说——

248
00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:07.780
It's a giant C.
它就是一个巨大的C形。

249
00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.440
Like, it's very curvy.
就是那种非常弯曲的形状。

250
00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:13.540
It looks like a curved spine, for those of you listening.
对于正在收听的各位，它看起来就像一根弯曲的脊椎。

251
00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:13.800
Yes, spiny.
没错，多刺的。

252
00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:14.720
It looks very spiny.
看起来确实很多刺。

253
00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:15.540
It looks like a spine.
看起来就像脊椎一样。

254
00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:20.760
And, yeah, so it looks like if you took an X-ray of your back, but—
而且，对，看起来就像你拍了张背部X光片，但是——

255
00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.880
And turned it into a leather sofa.
把它变成了一张皮沙发。

256
00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:23.720
A leather sofa.
一张皮沙发。

257
00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:29.860
But then the way the cushions look, it looks like if you chopped a recliner in three pieces,
但靠垫的样子，看起来就像是你把一把躺椅切成了三块，

258
00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:32.100
and then you just put them all in a row.
然后把它们排成了一排。

259
00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:35.460
Tons of mini, like, spine recliners.
全是那种迷你的、脊椎状的躺椅。

260
00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.660
Today's podcast is sponsored by DeSede Sofas.
今天的播客由DeSede沙发赞助。

261
00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.120
It is definitely not.
绝对不是。

262
00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:43.180
Sorry.
抱歉。

263
00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.100
Sorry, DeSede.
抱歉，DeSede。

264
00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:45.100
Or DeSed.
或者叫DeSed。

265
00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:45.900
We don't know what—
我们不知道——

266
00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:46.520
Oh, we're saying it wrong.
噢，我们读错了。

267
00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:47.080
We don't know.
我们不知道。

268
00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:47.840
We don't know.
我们不知道。

269
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.800
What we know is that we won't be purchasing one of your sofas for so many reasons.
我们只知道，出于种种原因，我们不会去买你们的沙发。

270
00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:54.400
Sorry.
抱歉。

271
00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:59.940
I love that this Dwight storyline was inspired by a true-life event in Halstead's life.
我喜欢德怀特这条故事线，它是受Halstead现实生活中的一件事启发而来的。

272
00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.160
It was really funny, too.
而且真的很有趣。

273
00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:03.080
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

274
00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:04.300
He was so happy.
他当时太开心了。

275
00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.540
He was getting everything right.
他把一切都做对了。

276
00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:07.380
I really liked it.
我真的很喜欢。

277
00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:10.340
Should we move on to fast fact number three?
我们要进入第三个速览事实了吗？

278
00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.680
Yes, because it's so special.
好的，因为它太特别了。

279
00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:15.980
We love this letter that we got from Alicia H.
我们很喜欢这封来自威斯康星州梅诺明市Alicia H.的来信。

280
00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.320
in Meinong, Wisconsin.
在梅诺明，威斯康星州。

281
00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:21.720
She wrote to us because this is the fundraiser episode.
她写信给我们是因为这一集是关于筹款的。

282
00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:22.160
Yeah.
没错。

283
00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:27.140
And she is having a fundraiser for her local library.
她正在为当地的图书馆筹款。

284
00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:32.360
Alicia said the building that the library is housed in was put up for sale last summer,
Alicia说图书馆所在的建筑去年夏天被挂牌出售了，

285
00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.600
and the community is working really hard to save the library.
社区正在努力拯救这座图书馆。

286
00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:40.200
She said most of the families that the library serves are below the poverty line,
她说图书馆服务的家庭大多处于贫困线以下，

287
00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:43.080
and the library has so many wonderful prograMs.
而且图书馆有很多很棒的项目。

288
00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:45.940
Her own four kids beg her to go all the time.
她自己的四个孩子总是缠着她要去图书馆。

289
00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:47.240
It's like their second home.
那里就像他们的第二个家。

290
00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:50.760
And she said that she would really like us to help support the library.
她说她真的很希望我们能帮忙支持这座图书馆。

291
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.660
She will even buy us tacos.
她甚至愿意请我们吃塔可。

292
00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.000
Well, Alicia, we loved your letter.
嗯，Alicia，我们很喜欢你的来信。

293
00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:00.280
We loved learning about your local library, which is 100% run by volunteers.
我们很高兴了解到你的当地图书馆，它完全是由志愿者运营的。

294
00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:00.960
Yes.
是的。

295
00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:05.880
If you go to their website, you can learn so much about what this library does for its community.
如果你访问他们的网站，就能了解到这座图书馆为社区做了多少贡献。

296
00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:10.320
It's a small community, and for those of you that live in small towns,
这是一个小社区，对于那些住在小镇的人来说，

297
00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:14.600
you know that the library can be such a wonderful place to go with your kids,
你们都知道图书馆是一个带孩子去的好地方，

298
00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:19.040
and you have access to things you might not be able to have at home or afford.
而且你们可以接触到在家里可能无法拥有或负担得起的东西。

299
00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.740
Very well said, Angela.
说得太好了，Angela。

300
00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:25.560
Well, Alicia, each year, Office Ladies does some annual giving,
那么，Alicia，每年《Office Ladies》都会进行一些年度捐赠，

301
00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:28.940
and we are adding your library to our list this year.
今年我们也会把你们的图书馆加入到我们的名单中。

302
00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.100
We're going to make a donation.
我们打算捐一笔款。

303
00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:30.500
Yep.
没错。

304
00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:36.100
We're also going to send you a signed copy of The Office BFFs and The Actor's Life for the library.
我们还会给图书馆寄去一本签名版的《办公室死党》和《演员人生》。

305
00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:37.260
Love it.
太棒了。

306
00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.140
And speaking of our annual giving,
说到我们每年的捐赠，

307
00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:44.640
this year we are also giving to Black Girls Code, AMSCI, and Lyday Haiti.
今年我们还向“黑人女孩编程”、AMSCI和Lyday海地组织进行了捐赠。

308
00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.880
Lyday Haiti is the organization that Rainn Wilson and his wife, Holiday Rinehorn, started.
Lyday海地是雷恩·威尔森和他妻子霍利迪·莱恩霍恩创办的组织。

309
00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:56.340
And you recently went to a fundraiser with Steve Carell for Lyday Haiti that was hosted by Rainn, right?
你最近是不是和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔一起参加了雷恩举办的Lyday海地筹款活动？

310
00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.020
We did.
是的。

311
00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:58.040
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

312
00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:01.100
And Rainn put together sort of this, quote-unquote, dinner party.
雷恩组织了一场所谓的“晚宴”。

313
00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:02.780
Amazing.
太神奇了。

314
00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:03.560
Right?
