00:27:05.990 --> 00:27:07.910
She wants a friend in the office.
她想在办公室里交个朋友。

638
00:27:08.150 --> 00:27:08.410
Yes.
是的。

639
00:27:09.070 --> 00:27:11.150
The fundraiser is now underway.
筹款活动现在开始了。

640
00:27:11.250 --> 00:27:14.630
We're going to see Angela in her outfit.
我们要看到安吉拉的装扮了。

641
00:27:15.290 --> 00:27:19.010
She's very much wanting to play the part of the senator's wife here.
她非常想在这里扮演好参议员夫人的角色。

642
00:27:19.810 --> 00:27:23.670
Robert California walks up and is interrupted by Andy.
罗伯特·加州走过来，被安迪打断了。

643
00:27:24.130 --> 00:27:27.950
And lady, I just wanted you to know this little introduction when Robert walks up.
还有，女士，我只是想让你知道罗伯特走过来时的这段小介绍。

644
00:27:28.050 --> 00:27:31.370
And Angela greets him and is like, the senator and I just wanted to say hello.
安吉拉迎接他，就像是说，参议员和我只是想来打个招呼。

645
00:27:31.690 --> 00:27:32.970
You know, she's doing like that.
你知道，她就是那样做的。

646
00:27:32.970 --> 00:27:34.390
That was all improvised.
那全是即兴发挥的。

647
00:27:34.590 --> 00:27:34.890
Oh.
哦。

648
00:27:35.290 --> 00:27:38.710
All it said in the script is that everyone says, hi, good to see you.
剧本里只写了每个人都说，嗨，很高兴见到你。

649
00:27:39.430 --> 00:27:39.930
Oh.
哦。

650
00:27:40.550 --> 00:27:41.590
Well, well done.
嗯，干得漂亮。

651
00:27:41.590 --> 00:27:42.450
I liked it.
我很喜欢。

652
00:27:42.590 --> 00:27:45.630
I was so delighted by this episode.
这一集让我感到非常开心。

653
00:27:45.770 --> 00:27:51.230
I just love it when Angela Martin thinks she's fancy and is trying to be fancy.
我就是喜欢安吉拉·马丁自以为很时髦、努力装作时髦的样子。

654
00:27:51.490 --> 00:27:56.550
And every single moment, I just wanted to find some little nugget of something to do
每一刻，我都想找点什么小细节来做，

655
00:27:56.550 --> 00:28:01.690
to show how high the stakes were for her to be the senator's wife at this event.
来展现她作为参议员夫人在这次活动中面临的巨大压力。

656
00:28:01.690 --> 00:28:05.550
Well, speaking of fancy, fan question from Katie Jo B.
说到时髦，有个来自印第安纳州凯蒂·乔·B的粉丝提问。

657
00:28:05.910 --> 00:28:07.130
in Indiana.
在印第安纳州。

658
00:28:07.510 --> 00:28:08.590
Hi, Katie Jo.
你好，凯蒂·乔。

659
00:28:09.210 --> 00:28:13.550
Angela, how did you feel about your zhuzhed hairdo at the fundraiser?
安吉拉，你对自己在筹款活动上那个精心打理的发型感觉如何？

660
00:28:13.710 --> 00:28:16.750
Did you have an extensive hair meeting like Jenna would have?
你像珍娜那样进行过详尽的发型会议吗？

661
00:28:17.090 --> 00:28:20.070
Did you love getting to smile so much in this episode?
这一集里能笑得那么多，你喜欢吗？

662
00:28:21.610 --> 00:28:23.730
You know, it was nice to smile.
你知道，能笑一笑真好。

663
00:28:24.090 --> 00:28:27.750
There is one scene, I will tell you, Katie, where I didn't get to smile.
凯蒂，我得告诉你，有一个场景我没能笑出来。

664
00:28:27.750 --> 00:28:35.010
It got deleted, but we did shoot it where I completely lose it because Andy is ruining
那段被删了，但我们确实拍过，当时我彻底崩溃了，因为安迪毁了

665
00:28:35.010 --> 00:28:35.850
my event.
我的活动。

666
00:28:36.950 --> 00:28:37.470
Yes.
没错。

667
00:28:37.470 --> 00:28:39.950
I go to the center and I'm like, he's ruining it.
我走到中心，我说，他把一切都毁了。

668
00:28:40.030 --> 00:28:41.030
And I'm just like upset.
我当时真的很难过。

669
00:28:41.430 --> 00:28:45.890
But for the most part, I got to smile this whole week, which was lovely.
但总的来说，这一周我大部分时间都在笑，这很棒。

670
00:28:46.110 --> 00:28:48.670
And we did have a very extensive hair meeting.
而且我们确实进行了一次非常详尽的发型会议。

671
00:28:48.670 --> 00:28:55.630
I remember the vision they wanted is that Angela Martin wants to be like Jackie Kennedy, right?
我记得他们想要的构想是，安吉拉·马丁想成为杰奎琳·肯尼迪那样的人，对吧？

672
00:28:56.030 --> 00:29:01.170
She wants that sort of bouffant hair that flipped out at the end, you know?
她想要那种发尾外翻的蓬松发型，你懂的？

673
00:29:01.690 --> 00:29:03.890
So yeah, that was our whole look.
所以，是的，那就是我们整体的造型。

674
00:29:04.050 --> 00:29:04.770
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

675
00:29:04.870 --> 00:29:06.610
You guys had a story behind the hairdo.
你们对这个发型还有一段故事背景。

676
00:29:06.730 --> 00:29:06.950
Yes.
是的。

677
00:29:07.050 --> 00:29:11.790
And this is the second time that Angela Martin has tried to look like Jackie Kennedy.
而且这已经是安吉拉·马丁第二次尝试模仿杰奎琳·肯尼迪了。

678
00:29:12.130 --> 00:29:12.930
You remember?
你还记得吗？

679
00:29:12.950 --> 00:29:14.850
She wore the pillbox hat.
她在菲利斯的婚礼上戴了药盒帽。

680
00:29:15.050 --> 00:29:15.270
Yes.
是的。

681
00:29:15.490 --> 00:29:17.090
And the blue suit to Phyllis's wedding.
还有那套蓝色套装。

682
00:29:17.090 --> 00:29:23.350
Something that's interesting to me is, would Angela support the Kennedy politics or it's
让我觉得有趣的是，安吉拉会支持肯尼迪的政治主张吗，还是

683
00:29:23.350 --> 00:29:24.370
just the fashion?
仅仅是因为时尚？

684
00:29:26.050 --> 00:29:28.050
That I'm not sure about.
这一点我不确定。

685
00:29:28.730 --> 00:29:30.870
It's an interesting choice of role model.
这是一个有趣的榜样选择。

686
00:29:31.070 --> 00:29:35.930
I'm surprised that she doesn't fashion herself after Nancy Reagan.
我很惊讶她没有把自己打扮成南希·里根的样子。

687
00:29:36.170 --> 00:29:38.910
Well, you know, she was Nancy Reagan for Halloween.
嗯，你知道，她万圣节时扮过南希·里根。

688
00:29:39.370 --> 00:29:40.210
This is true.
这倒是真的。

689
00:29:40.350 --> 00:29:42.950
I think she just wants to be a politician's wife.
我觉得她只是想当个政客的妻子。

690
00:29:43.150 --> 00:29:43.450
Yes.
是的。

691
00:29:43.530 --> 00:29:44.330
She doesn't care.
她不在乎。

692
00:29:44.330 --> 00:29:45.130
She doesn't care.
她不在乎。

693
00:29:45.210 --> 00:29:45.910
The political affiliation.
政治立场什么的。

694
00:29:46.050 --> 00:29:46.490
That's right.
没错。

695
00:29:46.490 --> 00:29:50.110
She just, if you have a good suit or a nice hat, she's going to try it out.
她只是，只要你有好看的套装或漂亮的帽子，她就会尝试一下。

696
00:29:50.390 --> 00:29:53.210
I've got a location breakdown for this banquet hall.
我这里有这个宴会厅的拍摄地点明细。

697
00:29:53.410 --> 00:29:58.810
We got a fan question from Haley in Austin, Texas asking, where were the fundraiser scenes
我们收到一个来自德克萨斯州奥斯汀的粉丝海莉的提问，问筹款活动的场景是在哪里

698
00:29:58.810 --> 00:29:59.270
shot?
拍摄的？

699
00:29:59.830 --> 00:30:03.170
At five minutes and three seconds, there's a shot of the outside of the building.
在五分零三秒处，有一个建筑物外观的镜头。

700
00:30:03.410 --> 00:30:06.450
Is that also the actual building that the scenes were shot in?
那也是实际拍摄这些场景的建筑物吗？

701
00:30:06.450 --> 00:30:08.370
These are very savvy questions.
这些问题问得非常内行。

702
00:30:08.710 --> 00:30:10.290
This is a long time listener.
这是一位老听众了。

703
00:30:10.630 --> 00:30:13.150
Haley knows that it could be different places.
海莉知道这可能是不同的地方。

704
00:30:13.430 --> 00:30:13.790
That's right.
没错。

705
00:30:14.330 --> 00:30:16.250
I asked Steve Burgess about this.
我问过史蒂夫·伯吉斯这件事。

706
00:30:16.390 --> 00:30:22.170
He said, we shot the ballroom fundraiser scenes at the Warner Center Marriott in Woodland Hills.
他说，我们在伍德兰希尔斯的华纳中心万豪酒店拍摄了舞厅筹款活动的场景。

707
00:30:22.750 --> 00:30:24.410
We were there for two days.
我们在那里待了两天。

708
00:30:25.070 --> 00:30:30.510
Steve said that he remembers sending a camera crew outside one night to get an establishing shot,
史蒂夫说他记得有天晚上派摄制组去外面拍了一个定场镜头，

709
00:30:30.610 --> 00:30:33.070
but he couldn't find it anywhere on his schedule.
但他怎么也找不到拍摄日程表上有这一项。

710
00:30:33.070 --> 00:30:37.550
So it is very possible that we used like a stock footage shot of a hotel.
所以很有可能我们用的是酒店的库存素材镜头。

711
00:30:38.150 --> 00:30:44.230
So he's not totally sure, but we did go on location to shoot the fundraiser banquet scenes.
所以他也不完全确定，但我们确实去了外景地拍摄筹款宴会的场景。

712
00:30:45.070 --> 00:30:49.630
But either way, Steve Burgess said that the banner on the outside of the building,
但无论如何，史蒂夫·伯吉斯说大楼外面的横幅，

713
00:30:49.630 --> 00:30:51.070
that was added in poSt.
那是后期加上去的。

714
00:30:51.230 --> 00:30:53.790
We did not actually hang a banner on a building.
我们并没有真的在建筑物上挂横幅。

715
00:30:54.490 --> 00:30:56.130
Andy is now going to have a talking head.
安迪现在要进行一段采访独白了。

716
00:30:56.350 --> 00:30:57.170
He says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

717
00:30:57.310 --> 00:30:58.270
Where do I look?
我该看哪儿？

718
00:30:58.470 --> 00:31:01.070
You know, it's been so long since I've done one of these interviews.
你知道，我已经很久没做过这种采访了。

719
00:31:01.450 --> 00:31:01.730
Yeah.
是啊。

720
00:31:01.930 --> 00:31:02.150
Yeah.
是啊。

721
00:31:02.470 --> 00:31:03.130
How am I doing?
我表现得怎么样？

722
00:31:03.290 --> 00:31:04.090
I'm doing great.
我表现得很好。

723
00:31:04.930 --> 00:31:05.730
Red flag.
危险信号。

724
00:31:05.730 --> 00:31:07.890
I mean, there's so many red flags.
我是说，有太多的危险信号了。

725
00:31:08.690 --> 00:31:08.950
Yeah.
是啊。

726
00:31:09.170 --> 00:31:10.290
Well, just wait.
嗯，等着瞧吧。

727
00:31:10.530 --> 00:31:13.070
There's going to be a flag flurry coming up.
马上就会有一阵“信号雨”了。

728
00:31:13.270 --> 00:31:14.010
A flag flurry.
信号雨。

729
00:31:14.630 --> 00:31:17.110
Kevin and Creed are going to check out the auction table.
凯文和克里德要去查看拍卖桌。

730
00:31:17.550 --> 00:31:21.890
And that's when Dwight is going to come up and tell them that they're doing it all wrong,
就在那时，德怀特走过来告诉他们，他们全搞错了，

731
00:31:21.990 --> 00:31:22.730
that they're idiots.
说他们是白痴。

732
00:31:23.090 --> 00:31:23.230
Yeah.
是啊。

733
00:31:23.490 --> 00:31:25.890
They haven't guessed the correct price of anything.
他们对任何东西的竞拍价格都没猜对。

734
00:31:26.490 --> 00:31:30.250
And Kevin tries to correct Dwight, but Dwight is just taking over.
凯文试图纠正德怀特，但德怀特直接接管了局面。

735
00:31:30.450 --> 00:31:32.870
He's just writing down a bunch of amounts.
他就在那儿写下一堆金额。

736
00:31:32.870 --> 00:31:34.490
And Kevin's like, okay, fine.
凯文心想，好吧，行吧。

737
00:31:34.490 --> 00:31:39.070
Kevin has a talking head where he says, Dwight doesn't understand what a silent auction is,
凯文有一段采访独白，他说，德怀特根本不懂什么是无声拍卖，

738
00:31:39.190 --> 00:31:41.810
which means he's the stupid guy in the office.
这意味着他是办公室里的那个笨蛋。

739
00:31:42.050 --> 00:31:43.870
Up till now, they didn't have one.
在此之前，他们还没人当过笨蛋。

740
00:31:44.290 --> 00:31:47.550
Can I tell you, that was not the scripted talking head.
我能告诉你吗，那不是剧本里的采访独白。

741
00:31:47.710 --> 00:31:48.570
It wasn't?
不是吗？

742
00:31:48.710 --> 00:31:49.210
It wasn't.
不是。

743
00:31:49.350 --> 00:31:51.330
That was the candy bag alt.
那是糖果袋的备选方案。

744
00:31:51.750 --> 00:31:54.290
The scripted talking head was this.
剧本里的采访独白是这样的。

745
00:31:54.810 --> 00:31:55.150
Huh.
哈。

746
00:31:55.330 --> 00:31:56.610
I know more than Dwight.
我知道的比德怀特多。

747
00:31:56.910 --> 00:31:58.110
You know what they say.
你知道人们怎么说吗。

748
00:31:58.310 --> 00:32:00.510
Even a clock is right once a day.
即使是坏掉的钟一天也能准两次。

749
00:32:01.070 --> 00:32:01.590
Oh.
哦。

750
00:32:01.590 --> 00:32:03.930
And they went with the candy bag alt.
最后他们选用了糖果袋的备选方案。

751
00:32:04.070 --> 00:32:07.030
Which is very funny because the saying is that a clock is right twice a day.
这很有趣，因为俗话说钟表一天准两次。

752
00:32:07.210 --> 00:32:10.610
A broken clock is right twice a day.
坏掉的钟表一天准两次。

753
00:32:10.810 --> 00:32:10.970
Right?
对吧？

754
00:32:11.250 --> 00:32:12.110
Isn't that the saying?
俗话不是这么说的吗？

755
00:32:12.190 --> 00:32:12.810
I don't know.
我不知道。

756
00:32:12.930 --> 00:32:17.130
But yeah, I thought this was a great example of when they actually went with one of the
不过确实，我觉得这是一个很好的例子，说明他们实际上选用了其中一个

757
00:32:17.130 --> 00:32:20.050
alts and didn't use the one that was in the shooting draft.
备选方案，而没有使用拍摄剧本里的那个。

758
00:32:20.410 --> 00:32:25.650
Well, I really like the detail of seeing Dwight guessing prices in the background of Kevin's
嗯，我真的很喜欢在凯文的采访镜头背景里看到德怀特在猜价格的细节，我去查了剧本，发现那并不是剧本里写的。

759
00:32:25.650 --> 00:32:29.370
talking head, and I went to the script, and I noticed that that was not scripted.
那是戴夫·罗杰斯导演的选择，我非常喜欢。

760
00:32:29.470 --> 00:32:33.250
That was a directing choice by Dave Rogers, and I absolutely loved it.
这对我来说确实增加了那一刻的真实感。

761
00:32:33.310 --> 00:32:35.510
It really added to the realism of the moment for me.
你知道，我丈夫非常非常擅长猜东西的价格。

762
00:32:35.950 --> 00:32:40.410
You know, my husband is very, very good at guessing prices of things.
就像他在《价格猜猜猜》节目里肯定会大杀四方？

763
00:32:40.790 --> 00:32:42.810
Like he would kill it on The Prices Right?
他绝对会大杀四方。

764
00:32:42.810 --> 00:32:43.790
He would kill it.
我上过《价格猜猜猜》。

765
00:32:43.910 --> 00:32:45.250
I went on The Prices Right.
我没能上台，但那是我刚搬到洛杉矶的时候。

766
00:32:45.250 --> 00:32:48.210
I didn't make it up on the stage, but when I first moved to L.A.
你在观众席里？

767
00:32:48.330 --> 00:32:49.230
You were in the audience?
对，我和两个朋友排了几个小时的队。

768
00:32:49.230 --> 00:32:53.330
Yeah, I waited in line for hours with two of my friends.
我拿到了写着我名字的小名牌。

769
00:32:53.710 --> 00:32:56.730
I got the little price tag with my name on it.
上面写着瑞吉娜，因为那是我的法定姓名。

770
00:32:56.730 --> 00:32:58.950
It said Regina, because that's my legal name.
他们必须在名牌上写你的法定姓名。

771
00:32:59.030 --> 00:33:01.250
They have to put your legal name on your price tag.
所以我坐在观众席里，尽我所能挥手，试图上台。

772
00:33:01.650 --> 00:33:07.790
And so I sat in the audience, and I did my best to like wave and try to get up on stage.
我真的很想上去。

773
00:33:08.230 --> 00:33:09.790
I really wanted to be on.
我想赢钱来付房租之类的。

774
00:33:09.990 --> 00:33:13.130
I wanted to win money to like pay for my apartment.
嗯，确实。

775
00:33:13.350 --> 00:33:13.830
Well, yeah.
因为我刚搬到这里。

776
00:33:14.010 --> 00:33:14.970
Because I just moved here.
但你可能只会赢到一辆摩托艇之类的东西。

777
00:33:15.090 --> 00:33:17.430
But you probably just would have won like a jet ski.
我知道。

778
00:33:17.730 --> 00:33:18.390
I know.
然后你会想，我有两辆摩托艇能干什么？

779
00:33:18.390 --> 00:33:21.350
And then you're like, what do I do with two jet skis?
好吧，可怜的帕姆知道生活中拥有两辆她不想要的摩托艇是什么下场。

780
00:33:21.510 --> 00:33:26.710
Well, poor Pam knows the fate of having two jet skis in her life that she doesn't want.
但你知道那些事吗？

781
00:33:27.110 --> 00:33:28.590
But you know those things?
我听说如果你赢了实际的奖品，比如洗衣机、烘干机或摩托艇之类的，

782
00:33:28.590 --> 00:33:33.470
I heard that if you win like an actual prize, like a washer dryer or jet ski or something,
在你拿到奖品之前，你必须先交税。

783
00:33:33.650 --> 00:33:37.490
before you can get your prize, you have to pay the taxes.
所以如果你赢了两辆价值约7000美元的摩托艇，你得先交税

784
00:33:38.310 --> 00:33:44.110
So if you win two jet skis that are worth like $7,000, first you have to pay the taxes
才能拿到你的摩托艇。

785
00:33:44.710 --> 00:33:46.270
before you get your jet skis.
所以你会收到一张账单。

786
00:33:46.350 --> 00:33:47.570
So you get like a bill.
是的。

787
00:33:48.510 --> 00:33:48.950
Yeah.
但我认为你也可以，我相信是这样。

788
00:33:49.230 --> 00:33:51.390
But I think you can also, I believe.
你可以直接说，我能只要现金价值吗？

789
