00:46:40.860 --> 00:46:42.360
You got to forget about Dunder Mifflin.
你得忘了邓德·米夫林公司。

1106
00:46:42.500 --> 00:46:44.180
And that's where the scene ended.
场景到这里就结束了。

1107
00:46:44.380 --> 00:46:45.480
But there was more.
但其实还有更多内容。

1108
00:46:45.800 --> 00:46:49.180
Oh, good, because we got a fan mail flurry about this scene.
哦，太好了，因为我们收到了很多关于这个场景的粉丝来信。

1109
00:46:49.400 --> 00:46:50.220
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

1110
00:46:50.380 --> 00:46:50.580
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

1111
00:46:50.780 --> 00:46:53.020
Jason T from Houston, Texas says,
来自德克萨斯州休斯顿的杰森·T说，

1112
00:46:53.140 --> 00:46:57.340
It seems odd that David Wallace appears without others noticing him.
大卫·华莱士出现时竟然没人注意到他，这看起来很奇怪。

1113
00:46:57.830 --> 00:46:59.900
It's not like the banquet room is packed.
宴会厅里又不是挤满了人。

1114
00:47:00.280 --> 00:47:02.780
Did some other things happen off camera?
镜头之外还发生了什么别的事吗？

1115
00:47:02.900 --> 00:47:06.280
I mean, you'd assume Jim would spend some time catching up with David Wallace.
我是说，你本以为吉姆会花点时间和大卫·华莱士叙叙旧。

1116
00:47:06.660 --> 00:47:08.640
And Teresa B from New Jersey said,
来自新泽西州的特蕾莎·B说，

1117
00:47:08.700 --> 00:47:11.880
Are there deleted scenes that help explain David Wallace's presence?
有没有什么删减片段能解释大卫·华莱士为什么会出现在那儿？

1118
00:47:12.740 --> 00:47:14.260
Hoping Angela can come through.
希望安吉拉能给出答案。

1119
00:47:14.880 --> 00:47:19.140
Well, Teresa, Jason, I have a little something here that might explain it.
好吧，特蕾莎，杰森，我这儿确实有些东西或许能解释清楚。

1120
00:47:19.420 --> 00:47:25.280
So the scene was scripted that Andy is actually exiting the restroom when he bumps into David Wallace.
剧本里原本写的是安迪从洗手间出来时撞见了大卫·华莱士。

1121
00:47:25.280 --> 00:47:28.040
And the whole top of the scene is the same.
场景的前半部分是一样的。

1122
00:47:28.260 --> 00:47:29.900
But then David at the end says,
但大卫在最后说，

1123
00:47:30.720 --> 00:47:32.580
Point is, forget those guys.
重点是，忘了那些人吧。

1124
00:47:32.780 --> 00:47:33.220
Move on.
向前看。

1125
00:47:33.380 --> 00:47:34.820
And then Andy would have said,
然后安迪本该说，

1126
00:47:35.100 --> 00:47:35.560
Move on.
向前看。

1127
00:47:35.560 --> 00:47:37.500
I'm partying with them tonight.
我今晚还要和他们一起聚会呢。

1128
00:47:38.200 --> 00:47:39.200
David says,
大卫说，

1129
00:47:39.700 --> 00:47:39.960
Really?
真的吗？

1130
00:47:40.180 --> 00:47:40.540
Wow.
哇。

1131
00:47:40.700 --> 00:47:40.960
Okay.
好吧。

1132
00:47:41.200 --> 00:47:43.360
That sounds very awkward to me.
这听起来让我觉得很尴尬。

1133
00:47:43.580 --> 00:47:47.140
I don't think I would have come if I knew Dunder Mifflin was coming.
如果我知道邓德·米夫林的人会来，我可能就不会来了。

1134
00:47:47.740 --> 00:47:47.960
Hmm.
嗯。

1135
00:47:48.600 --> 00:47:50.040
Then there's a beat and he goes,
然后停顿了一下，他说，

1136
00:47:50.140 --> 00:47:51.420
Hey, but you know what?
嘿，但你知道吗？

1137
00:47:51.480 --> 00:47:54.360
Make sure you tell everyone I sold suck it for a ton of money.
一定要告诉大家我把“吸它”卖了一大笔钱。

1138
00:47:54.460 --> 00:47:54.680
Okay?
好吗？

1139
00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:55.520
See ya.
再见。

1140
00:47:55.820 --> 00:47:57.180
And then he walks away.
然后他就走开了。

1141
00:47:57.660 --> 00:48:01.160
So it sounds like to me he doesn't want to see the Dunder Mifflin crew.
所以听起来他并不想见到邓德·米夫林的员工。

1142
00:48:01.400 --> 00:48:03.920
He wouldn't have even come if he knew they were going to be there.
如果他知道他们会去，他根本就不会来。

1143
00:48:04.140 --> 00:48:06.000
How does he not know they're going to be there?
他怎么会不知道他们会去呢？

1144
00:48:06.180 --> 00:48:09.940
Isn't it like common knowledge that Angela is the senator's wife?
安吉拉是参议员夫人的事难道不是众所周知的吗？

1145
00:48:10.630 --> 00:48:14.200
And also, I have to agree with Jason from Houston.
而且，我也同意休斯顿的杰森的看法。

1146
00:48:14.480 --> 00:48:16.380
This is not a large room.
这房间并不大。

1147
00:48:16.600 --> 00:48:20.060
I mean, I can see everybody clearly.
我是说，我可以清楚地看到每一个人。

1148
00:48:20.400 --> 00:48:22.000
Where is David sitting?
大卫坐在哪儿呢？

1149
00:48:22.340 --> 00:48:28.540
What about all of the hobnobbing that happened maybe pre-dinner or at the auction tables?
那在晚餐前或者在拍卖桌旁发生的那些社交寒暄呢？

1150
00:48:28.920 --> 00:48:31.360
There's so much hobnobbing at these things.
这种场合里总是有那么多的社交寒暄。

1151
00:48:31.600 --> 00:48:32.640
Yes, there is.
是的，确实有。

1152
00:48:33.100 --> 00:48:33.860
I know.
我知道。

1153
00:48:33.960 --> 00:48:37.100
Well, I think of the Dunder Mifflin crew, he would have said hi to Jim.
嗯，我觉得如果是邓德·米夫林的人，他应该会跟吉姆打招呼的。

1154
00:48:37.420 --> 00:48:37.840
Yes.
是的。

1155
00:48:37.840 --> 00:48:42.060
And while it might have been scripted that this scene takes place outside of a restroom,
虽然剧本里可能写了这场戏发生在洗手间外面，

1156
00:48:42.200 --> 00:48:43.820
that was definitely not clear to me.
但我完全没看出来。

1157
00:48:44.320 --> 00:48:47.340
It looks like he's just right in the ballroom.
看起来他就像是在宴会厅里一样。

1158
00:48:47.960 --> 00:48:48.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1159
00:48:48.460 --> 00:48:54.260
Well, I found it interesting in the script that David wouldn't have come if he knew the Dunder Mifflin crew was there.
嗯，我觉得剧本里有一点很有意思，大卫要是知道邓德·米夫林的人在场，他根本就不会来。

1160
00:48:54.580 --> 00:48:56.400
What's his beef with the Dunder Mifflin crew?
他和邓德·米夫林的人有什么过节吗？

1161
00:48:56.880 --> 00:48:58.000
He's moved on.
他已经翻篇了。

1162
00:48:58.240 --> 00:48:58.640
Okay.
好吧。

1163
00:48:58.640 --> 00:48:59.380
He's moved on.
他已经翻篇了。

1164
00:48:59.900 --> 00:49:03.000
Well, now Nellie is going to try to bond with Daryl.
好了，现在奈莉要试着和达里尔套近乎了。

1165
00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:09.400
She's complaining about the food, said she'd give anything for just a burger or pizza pie or whatever else they like.
她在抱怨食物，说她愿意为了一个汉堡、披萨或者他们喜欢的其他什么东西付出一切。

1166
00:49:09.700 --> 00:49:11.120
Daryl suggests tacos.
达里尔提议吃塔可。

1167
00:49:11.740 --> 00:49:16.120
And it is so clear that Nellie has no idea what a taco is.
很明显，奈莉根本不知道塔可是什么。

1168
00:49:16.680 --> 00:49:16.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1169
00:49:17.240 --> 00:49:19.920
She has a talking head where she says she's never had a taco.
她有个单人采访镜头，说她从来没吃过塔可。

1170
00:49:20.680 --> 00:49:23.380
She's hoping that they're not slimy and don't have eyes.
她还在祈祷那玩意儿别是黏糊糊的，也别长着眼睛。

1171
00:49:23.380 --> 00:49:31.780
I would like to say that Nellie pining away for different food really tracks if you look at everybody's plate.
我想说的是，如果你看看每个人的盘子，奈莉对其他食物的渴望确实是有迹可循的。

1172
00:49:32.360 --> 00:49:38.700
I only saw myself eating at the table, and I think I had requested a plate of vegetables,
我只看到自己在桌边吃东西，我想我当时要了一盘蔬菜，

1173
00:49:38.940 --> 00:49:42.960
but you'll notice that Jim's fish goes untouched the entire episode.
但你会发现吉姆的那份鱼整集都没动过。

1174
00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:45.200
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

1175
00:49:45.560 --> 00:49:45.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1176
00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:48.880
I could see how maybe Nellie wanted something else.
我能理解为什么奈莉可能想吃点别的。

1177
00:49:48.880 --> 00:49:56.560
I will tell you what's pretty gross is if you do, like, a 12-hour scene and you have, like, a meatloaf or something on a plate in front of you
我告诉你什么才叫恶心，如果你拍一场12小时的戏，面前放着一块肉饼之类的东西，

1178
00:49:56.560 --> 00:50:00.960
that you have to push around for 12 hours and pretend to eat.
你得在那儿推来推去12个小时，假装在吃。

1179
00:50:01.280 --> 00:50:11.460
I couldn't believe that I don't have memories of the fish that was on John's plate for all those scenes with me and John and Oscar
我简直不敢相信，我和约翰还有奥斯卡拍了那么多场戏，我竟然对约翰盘子里的那条鱼一点印象都没有，

1180
00:50:11.460 --> 00:50:14.720
because it's just sitting there the whole time.
因为它就一直摆在那儿。

1181
00:50:14.860 --> 00:50:15.980
It never changes.
从来没变过。

1182
00:50:17.080 --> 00:50:21.440
Speaking of our table, Jim is going to return to the table, and guess what?
说到我们的桌子，吉姆要回座位了，你猜怎么着？

1183
00:50:21.520 --> 00:50:23.180
He got the senator's cell phone number, too.
他也拿到了参议员的手机号码。

1184
00:50:23.480 --> 00:50:24.040
Yeah, he did.
没错，他拿到了。

1185
00:50:24.400 --> 00:50:25.440
How about that, Oscar?
奥斯卡，你觉得呢？

1186
00:50:26.100 --> 00:50:28.540
Well, Oscar and Pam say Jim hasn't proven anything.
嗯，奥斯卡和帕姆说吉姆什么都没证明。

1187
00:50:29.140 --> 00:50:32.320
All he's proven is that maybe the senator thinks Jim is gay.
他唯一证明的就是参议员可能觉得吉姆是同性恋。

1188
00:50:32.540 --> 00:50:34.000
Then they make fun of Jim's shoes.
然后他们就开始取笑吉姆的鞋子。

1189
00:50:34.400 --> 00:50:36.260
They say no gay man would wear those shoes.
他们说没有哪个同性恋会穿那种鞋。

1190
00:50:36.920 --> 00:50:37.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1191
00:50:37.600 --> 00:50:39.140
Jim's like, you bought me these shoes.
吉姆说，这鞋还是你们给我买的呢。

1192
00:50:39.620 --> 00:50:42.460
Like, why are you making fun of my shoes?
就像是，你们为什么要取笑我的鞋？

1193
00:50:42.460 --> 00:50:43.580
Why are you selling my shoes that you bought me?
你们为什么要卖掉你们给我买的鞋？

1194
00:50:43.720 --> 00:50:44.560
It was very funny.
这太搞笑了。

1195
00:50:45.240 --> 00:50:47.760
Robert California is now going to take to the podium.
罗伯特·加州现在要走上讲台了。

1196
00:50:48.400 --> 00:50:53.340
He's going to speak about saving elderly dogs, who he calls heroes.
他要发表关于拯救老年犬的演讲，他称它们为英雄。

1197
00:50:53.740 --> 00:50:55.320
Fan catch from Timothy B.
来自德国的蒂莫西·B的粉丝发现。

1198
00:50:55.540 --> 00:50:56.160
in Germany.
背景细节捕捉。

1199
00:50:56.520 --> 00:50:57.640
Background catch.
背景细节捕捉。

1200
00:50:58.040 --> 00:51:03.840
When the senator is introducing Robert California, you can see Angela mouth along the words.
当参议员介绍罗伯特·加州时，你可以看到安吉拉在跟着对口型。

1201
00:51:04.100 --> 00:51:05.940
Yes, that was a choice I made.
是的，那是我的一个选择。

1202
00:51:06.000 --> 00:51:06.700
I improvised that.
那是我的即兴发挥。

1203
00:51:06.820 --> 00:51:08.720
I just figured she would know his whole introduction.
我只是觉得她应该知道他完整的介绍词。

1204
00:51:08.720 --> 00:51:12.700
There's actually more in deleted scenes where he gets up and speaks.
其实在删减片段里还有更多内容，他站起来发言了。

1205
00:51:12.860 --> 00:51:17.960
And every time he does, the camera would find me and I would be saying all of his lines with him.
每次他发言时，镜头都会切到我，我都会跟着他一起说出所有的台词。

1206
00:51:17.960 --> 00:51:19.920
I like that choice that tracks.
我喜欢那个选择，这很符合逻辑。

1207
00:51:20.240 --> 00:51:20.440
Thank you.
谢谢。

1208
00:51:20.720 --> 00:51:22.420
We had a fan question from Megan W.
我们收到了一位来自马萨诸塞州的粉丝Megan W.的提问。

1209
00:51:22.460 --> 00:51:33.740
in Massachusetts who wanted to know, Angela, were there any deleted scenes or talking head alts during which Angela comments about this fundraiser being for dogs and not cats?
她想知道，安吉拉，有没有什么删减片段或备选采访镜头，是安吉拉评论这次筹款活动是为狗而不是为猫举办的？

1210
00:51:33.740 --> 00:51:39.340
I was surprised Angela's talking head about the fundraiser didn't include any snide remark.
我很惊讶安吉拉关于筹款活动的采访镜头里竟然没有包含任何讽刺言论。

1211
00:51:40.860 --> 00:51:46.440
All we see is the side look that she gives to the dog during Robert California's speech.
我们看到的只有她在罗伯特·加利福尼亚演讲时，瞥向那只狗的一个眼神。

1212
00:51:46.720 --> 00:51:48.420
Megan, that's such a good question.
Megan，这真是个好问题。

1213
00:51:48.680 --> 00:51:55.580
You know, I think she was so pleased to be part of a fundraiser event with her politician husband.
你知道，我觉得她当时很高兴能和她身为政客的丈夫一起参加筹款活动。

1214
00:51:55.580 --> 00:52:03.460
And even though maybe it wasn't for anything she truly cares about, she still gets to be up front and center, right?
即使这可能不是她真正关心的事，但她依然能站在最显眼的位置，对吧？

1215
00:52:03.580 --> 00:52:06.400
So that's why I think there's no snarky comment in the talking head.
所以我认为这就是为什么采访镜头里没有尖酸刻薄的评论。

1216
00:52:06.780 --> 00:52:13.420
But there's only one mention of Angela Martin's attitude towards the event in the shooting draft.
但在拍摄剧本中，只有一处提到了安吉拉·马丁对这次活动的态度。

1217
00:52:13.420 --> 00:52:16.680
And it happens when the senator is introduced.
那是在参议员被介绍出场的时候。

1218
00:52:17.260 --> 00:52:21.400
In the script it said, Robert California says, why do we love dogs?
剧本里写着，罗伯特·加利福尼亚问，我们为什么爱狗？

1219
00:52:21.400 --> 00:52:26.480
And then there's this stage direction, angle on Angela, not buying the premise.
然后有一条舞台提示：镜头对准安吉拉，她不买账。

1220
00:52:28.220 --> 00:52:32.680
And I remember, like, when I read that, I was like, how do I convey that?
我记得当时读到这里时，我在想，我该怎么表现出来呢？

1221
00:52:32.800 --> 00:52:34.860
And then I just, there was a dog right next to me.
然后我刚好看到旁边有一只狗。

1222
00:52:34.940 --> 00:52:36.000
So I thought, oh, I'll look at it.
于是我想，哦，我就盯着它看吧。

1223
00:52:36.060 --> 00:52:36.820
I'll roll my eyes.
我翻个白眼。

1224
00:52:36.920 --> 00:52:37.740
I'll be grossed out.
表现出我很反感的样子。

1225
00:52:37.920 --> 00:52:40.500
The true Angela does bleed through.
真正的安吉拉确实流露出来了。

1226
00:52:40.600 --> 00:52:42.220
Yes, just for a little moment.
是的，就那一小会儿。

1227
00:52:43.400 --> 00:52:46.760
Andy is going to interrupt Robert California's speech.
安迪要打断罗伯特·加利福尼亚的演讲。

1228
00:52:46.760 --> 00:52:56.160
And he is going to volunteer to take all of the elderly dogs home with him and, I guess, adopt them.
他要主动提出把所有的老年犬都带回家，我想，就是领养它们。

1229
00:52:56.400 --> 00:52:57.480
All of them.
全部领养。

1230
00:52:57.900 --> 00:52:58.540
Yes.
是的。

1231
00:52:58.900 --> 00:53:00.500
It's so many dogs.
那可是好多狗啊。

1232
00:53:00.940 --> 00:53:02.740
Well, now we're going to see Andy.
好了，现在我们要看到安迪了。

1233
00:53:03.020 --> 00:53:09.780
He's with the animal welfare volunteer who's walking him through the different various needs of these dogs.
他和动物福利志愿者在一起，志愿者正在向他介绍这些狗的不同需求。

1234
00:53:09.780 --> 00:53:11.580
They all have special needs.
它们都有特殊需求。

1235
00:53:12.620 --> 00:53:16.820
One of the dogs, Kenny, is a therapy dog, and he's really bonding with Andy.
其中一只叫肯尼的狗是治疗犬，它和安迪相处得特别好。

1236
00:53:17.060 --> 00:53:19.500
And the animal welfare volunteer says, you know what?
动物福利志愿者说，你知道吗？

1237
00:53:19.600 --> 00:53:22.260
He must think you're in the midst of an emotional crisis.
它一定觉得你正处于情感危机中。

1238
00:53:23.360 --> 00:53:23.880
Yes.
是的。

1239
00:53:25.520 --> 00:53:29.560
Our animal welfare volunteer was played by Andrew Segunda.
我们的动物福利志愿者是由安德鲁·塞贡达饰演的。

1240
00:53:29.860 --> 00:53:33.460
He was a writer on Late Night with Conan O'Brien and the Goldbergs.
他曾是《柯南·奥布莱恩深夜秀》和《戈德堡一家》的编剧。

1241
00:53:33.460 --> 00:53:43.240
He also played Dr. Ewing in The League, and he co-hosts a Star Trek The Next Generation rewatch podcast called Star Trek The Next Conversation.
他还在《联盟》中饰演了尤因医生，并且是《星际迷航：下一代》重温播客《星际迷航：下一场对话》的联合主持人。

1242
00:53:43.600 --> 00:53:43.900
Oh.
哦。

1243
00:53:44.340 --> 00:53:48.160
I'll also have you know we did not shoot these scenes at the hotel.
我还要告诉你们，我们并没有在酒店拍摄这些场景。

1244
00:53:48.560 --> 00:53:54.120
Haley, who asked us about locations, this room was a set that we built on the warehouse stages.
海莉，你问过我们拍摄地点，这个房间是我们搭建在摄影棚里的布景。

1245
00:53:54.120 --> 00:53:57.380
And we also got a fan question from Katie Jo B.
我们还收到了来自印第安纳州的凯蒂·乔·B.

1246
00:53:57.540 --> 00:53:59.080
in Indiana and Nicole L.
和来自加拿大的妮可·L.的粉丝提问，

1247
00:53:59.280 --> 00:54:00.500
from Canada who said,
她们说，

1248
00:54:00.660 --> 00:54:03.820
please tell us everything about the senior dogs.
请告诉我们关于这些老年犬的一切。

1249
00:54:03.840 --> 00:54:07.020
Are they from the normal animal training rental company?
它们是来自普通的动物训练租赁公司吗？

1250
00:54:07.300 --> 00:54:11.980
Were all the dogs actors, or were any of them actual rescues at the time?
所有的狗都是演员，还是说其中有一些当时真的是救援犬？

1251
00:54:12.400 --> 00:54:15.020
Well, guys, all the dogs came through.
好了，各位，所有的狗狗都顺利完成了任务。

1252
00:54:15.200 --> 00:54:15.880
Bob done.
鲍勃做到了。

1253
00:54:16.420 --> 00:54:17.760
Not really a surprise there.
这倒不让人意外。

1254
00:54:17.940 --> 00:54:18.900
They were not rescues.
它们不是救援犬。

1255
00:54:19.040 --> 00:54:19.960
They were working dogs.
它们是工作犬。

1256
00:54:20.180 --> 00:54:23.520
We had three trainers to take care of the six dogs.
我们有三名训练师来照顾这六只狗。

1257
00:54:23.520 --> 00:54:29.160
They worked for two days, one day on this little set that we built, and one day at the Marriott.
它们工作了两天，一天是在我们搭建的这个小布景里，另一天是在万豪酒店。

1258
00:54:29.320 --> 00:54:33.180
And the total cost for the dogs and trainers was about $6,000.
狗狗和训练师的总费用大约是6000美元。

1259
00:54:33.760 --> 00:54:38.500
I also asked Steve Burgess if he had the doggy headshots for each of our dog actors.
我还问了史蒂夫·伯吉斯，他有没有我们每位狗狗演员的头像照。

1260
00:54:38.840 --> 00:54:39.940
And he did.
他确实有。

1261
00:54:40.720 --> 00:54:42.480
Bella was played by Scout.
贝拉是由斯考特扮演的。

1262
00:54:42.900 --> 00:54:47.260
And the other dog actors were Lucy, Monkey, Langley, Bullet, and Duke.
其他的狗狗演员分别是露西、猴子、兰利、子弹和杜克。

1263
00:54:47.800 --> 00:54:49.800
I will put their headshots in stories.
我会把它们的头像照发到快拍里。

1264
00:54:49.800 --> 00:54:53.860
Steve said when they talked to the animal trainers about what each dog would have to do,
史蒂夫说，当他们和动物训练师讨论每只狗需要做什么时，

1265
00:54:54.080 --> 00:54:56.780
these were the dogs that they recommended for those roles.
这些就是他们为那些角色推荐的狗。

1266
00:54:57.060 --> 00:54:57.720
I see.
我明白了。

1267
00:54:57.840 --> 00:54:58.440
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

1268
00:54:58.860 --> 00:54:59.880
They were caSt.
它们是被选中的。

1269
00:54:59.900 --> 00:55:00.440
They had-
它们有——

1270
00:55:00.440 --> 00:55:01.080
Based on their abilities.
基于它们的能力。

1271
00:55:01.280 --> 00:55:02.560
Yes, they had their specialties.
是的，它们各有专长。

1272
00:55:03.120 --> 00:55:03.800
Oh, dear.
噢，天哪。

1273
00:55:03.800 --> 00:55:05.120
Guess what's going to happen now?
猜猜现在会发生什么？

1274
00:55:05.700 --> 00:55:08.640
The senator is going to give Meredith his cell phone number.
参议员要给梅雷迪思他的手机号码了。

1275
00:55:09.020 --> 00:55:11.000
Well, that blows Oscar's theory.
好吧，这下奥斯卡的理论被推翻了。

1276
00:55:11.240 --> 00:55:11.800
That's right.
没错。

1277
00:55:11.940 --> 00:55:12.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1278
00:55:12.480 --> 00:55:13.940
Jim still hasn't eaten his fish.
吉姆还没吃他的鱼。

1279
00:55:13.940 --> 00:55:14.700
Wish I tracked it.
真希望我记录下来了。

1280
00:55:15.120 --> 00:55:18.520
Oscar is now going to have a talking head where he says he's not disappointed that
奥斯卡现在要进行一段访谈，他说他并不失望，

1281
00:55:18.520 --> 00:55:20.180
Angela's husband wasn't hitting on him.
因为安吉拉的丈夫并没有在勾引他。

1282
00:55:20.320 --> 00:55:22.420
He'd have to be a monster to root for that.
如果支持那种事，那他得是个怪物。

1283
00:55:22.660 --> 00:55:24.920
A lonely, aging monster.
一个孤独、衰老的怪物。

1284
00:55:25.440 --> 00:55:26.580
Mm, poor Oscar.
嗯，可怜的奥斯卡。

1285
00:55:27.140 --> 00:55:31.060
Daryl returns with tacos, and Nellie doesn't know how to eat one.
达里尔带回了塔可饼，而奈莉不知道该怎么吃。

1286
00:55:31.400 --> 00:55:36.560
It's like she's, I don't know, scooping the ingredients into her mouth from the shell.
她看起来就像是，我不知道，在用壳把配料舀进嘴里。

1287
00:55:36.700 --> 00:55:38.220
She's not biting into the shell.
她没有直接咬那个壳。

1288
00:55:38.220 --> 00:55:44.620
We got a fan question from Jen G in Kentucky who said, I'm a theater professor, and I specialize
我们收到了来自肯塔基州珍·G的一位粉丝提问，她说，我是一名戏剧教授，专门研究

1289
00:55:44.620 --> 00:55:49.520
in women in comedy and improv, and this episode has one of my favorite bits of physical
喜剧和即兴表演中的女性，这一集有我全剧中最喜欢的肢体

1290
00:55:49.520 --> 00:55:53.900
clowning in the entire series, and it is when Nellie tries to eat a taco.
小丑表演片段之一，就是奈莉试图吃塔可饼的那一段。

1291
00:55:55.140 --> 00:56:00.140
I desperately need to know how she came to this bit, to what degree it was scripted,
我非常想知道她是怎么想到这个桥段的，它在多大程度上是剧本写的，

1292
00:56:00.140 --> 00:56:05.420
and to what degree it emerged from the magical mists of Catherine Tate's fabulous mind.
又在多大程度上是从凯瑟琳·塔特那美妙头脑的魔法迷雾中涌现出来的。

1293
00:56:05.420 --> 00:56:08.620
Well, Jen, this taco eating was scripted.
好吧，珍，这个吃塔可饼的桥段是写在剧本里的。

1294
00:56:08.820 --> 00:56:09.920
Here's what it said.
剧本上是这样写的。

1295
00:56:10.400 --> 00:56:15.120
Quote, Nellie picks up the taco, unsure how to eat it, then puts it to her mouth sideways
引用：奈莉拿起塔可饼，不知道怎么吃，然后把它横着放到嘴边，

1296
00:56:15.120 --> 00:56:18.600
with her finger pushes the filling down her throat.
用手指把馅料推进喉咙里。

1297
00:56:19.020 --> 00:56:20.860
And then this little bit got cut.
然后这一小段被剪掉了。

1298
00:56:21.080 --> 00:56:27.260
It said, Nellie holds the empty shell and looks around and says, savory, is there a plate
剧本上写着，奈莉拿着空壳环顾四周，说道，美味，有装

1299
00:56:27.260 --> 00:56:28.020
for the shells?
壳的盘子吗？

1300
00:56:29.820 --> 00:56:35.860
So, this was a combo platter of scripting, and also, though, of course, Catherine Tate's
所以，这既是剧本的功劳，当然，也少不了凯瑟琳·塔特的发挥。

1301
00:56:35.860 --> 00:56:38.000
interpretation of what was scripted.
对剧本内容的解读。

1302
00:56:38.260 --> 00:56:38.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1303
00:56:38.980 --> 00:56:43.700
Well, her attempt at trying to eat a taco, it tugs on Daryl's heartstrings.
嗯，她试图吃塔可饼的样子，触动了达里尔的心弦。

1304
00:56:43.960 --> 00:56:45.120
He's starting to soften.
他开始心软了。

1305
00:56:45.140 --> 00:56:47.680
He has a talking head, and he says she's trying.
他在采访中说，她确实在努力。

1306
00:56:48.020 --> 00:56:48.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1307
00:56:48.760 --> 00:56:50.920
It's time now to announce the auction winners.
现在是宣布拍卖获胜者的时候了。

1308
00:56:51.260 --> 00:56:52.360
Guess what, guys?
你们猜怎么着？

1309
00:56:52.480 --> 00:56:56.340
Dwight wins the first item, and the second, and the third.
德怀特赢得了第一件、第二件，还有第三件拍品。

1310
00:56:56.340 --> 00:56:57.880
Well, you know what?
好吧，你知道吗？

1311
00:56:57.960 --> 00:56:58.320
Guess what?
猜猜怎么着？

1312
00:56:58.420 --> 00:56:59.200
He's won them all.
他把所有的都赢走了。

1313
00:56:59.660 --> 00:57:00.200
Yes.
没错。

1314
00:57:00.300 --> 00:57:05.200
The emcee says, I'm going to save us some time, and just announced that Dwight Schrute
主持人说，为了节省时间，我直接宣布德怀特·舒鲁特

1315
00:57:05.200 --> 00:57:10.640
won everything, and they are so grateful for his donation of over $34,000.
赢得了所有拍品，他们非常感谢他捐赠了超过34000美元。

1316
00:57:11.120 --> 00:57:13.100
It's the largest they've ever received.
这是他们收到过最大的一笔捐款。

1317
00:57:13.640 --> 00:57:17.160
Thus begins a standing ovation started by Jim.
于是，由吉姆带头，全场起立鼓掌。

1318
00:57:17.360 --> 00:57:17.740
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1319
00:57:18.060 --> 00:57:22.880
It was scripted that Jim would start the ovation and yell speech, but I personally love
剧本里写的是吉姆带头鼓掌并大喊“演讲”，但我个人很喜欢

1320
00:57:22.880 --> 00:57:26.120
John's choice of also being the last person standing and clapping.
约翰选择成为最后一个站着鼓掌的人。

1321
00:57:26.900 --> 00:57:32.520
Oh, I feel like I should let you know our emcee guest star was played by Elizabeth Payne,
哦，我觉得应该告诉你们，我们的客串主持人是由伊丽莎白·佩恩饰演的，

1322
00:57:32.640 --> 00:57:35.800
who was our writer Halstead Sullivan's high school prom date.
她是我们编剧霍尔斯特德·沙利文的高中舞会舞伴。

1323
00:57:36.500 --> 00:57:36.780
Aw.
噢。

1324
00:57:37.060 --> 00:57:38.880
Halstead said he had nothing to do with her casting.
霍尔斯特德说她的选角和他没关系。

1325
00:57:39.100 --> 00:57:40.100
She's a working actor.
她是一名职业演员。

1326
00:57:40.260 --> 00:57:45.240
He didn't even know that she got cast on the show and was in this episode until they screened
他甚至不知道她被选中出演这部剧，也不知道她出现在这一集里，直到他们为编剧们

1327
00:57:45.240 --> 00:57:46.520
this episode for the writers.
放映这一集时才知道。

1328
00:57:46.800 --> 00:57:47.440
Come on.
得了吧。

1329
00:57:47.500 --> 00:57:47.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1330
00:57:47.760 --> 00:57:51.780
He said, you know, if you weren't the writer of the episode, you stayed in the writer's
他说，你知道，如果你不是这一集的编剧，你大部分时间都待在编剧

1331
00:57:51.780 --> 00:57:52.780
room most of the time.
室里。

1332
00:57:52.780 --> 00:57:53.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1333
00:57:53.200 --> 00:57:54.200
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

1334
00:57:54.600 --> 00:57:58.460
He said, Elizabeth is also a successful voice actress.
他说，伊丽莎白也是一位成功的配音演员。

1335
00:57:58.840 --> 00:58:02.480
She voiced the pre-crime voice in the Minority Report.
她在《少数派报告》里为“预知犯罪”系统配过音。

1336
00:58:03.020 --> 00:58:03.420
Oh.
哦。

1337
00:58:03.720 --> 00:58:04.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1338
00:58:04.620 --> 00:58:05.360
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1339
00:58:05.360 --> 00:58:10.700
And if you watched the first season of Ugly Betty, she played the mysterious masked woman
如果你看过《丑女贝蒂》第一季，她饰演了剧中那个神秘的蒙面女人。

1340
00:58:10.700 --> 00:58:11.380
on the show.
剧中有一个女人做了整形手术来改变身份，

1341
00:58:11.720 --> 00:58:16.000
I guess there was a woman on the show who had plastic surgery to change her identity and
没人知道她是谁。

1342
00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:17.160
no one knew who she was.
当她最终揭开面具时，是由丽贝卡·罗梅恩饰演的。

1343
00:58:17.500 --> 00:58:21.920
And when she was finally unmasked, she was played by Rebecca Romijn.
但在那之前，是伊丽莎白·佩恩演的。

1344
00:58:22.360 --> 00:58:25.460
But before that, it was Elizabeth Payne.
嗯。

1345
00:58:25.460 --> 00:58:25.980
Hmm.
好吧，现在德怀特要上去发表他的演讲了。

1346
00:58:26.560 --> 00:58:29.120
Well, now Dwight's going to go up and make his speech.
大家都在高喊：演讲，演讲。

1347
00:58:29.340 --> 00:58:31.140
Everyone's chanting, speech, speech.
他说他非常自豪能支持这个活动，钱对他来说不是问题。

1348
00:58:32.000 --> 00:58:37.540
He says he's really proud to support whatever this is and that money is no concern to him.
但这一切是从什么时候开始变得只谈钱了呢？

1349
00:58:37.920 --> 00:58:40.320
But when did it all become about money?
他正试图从中脱身。

1350
00:58:40.680 --> 00:58:42.160
He's trying to get out of it.
他正试图从中脱身。

1351
00:58:42.300 --> 00:58:42.540
Yes.
是的。

1352
00:58:42.640 --> 00:58:46.140
He says, what did we spend on the flower arrangements, the white wine spritzers?
他说，我们在鲜花布置和白葡萄酒汽酒上花了多少钱？

1353
00:58:46.360 --> 00:58:47.760
How many courses did they have tonight?
他们今晚吃了多少道菜？

1354
00:58:47.960 --> 00:58:49.220
Three, if they chose pudding.
三道，如果他们选了布丁的话。

1355
00:58:49.500 --> 00:58:51.440
And they should be ashamed of themselves.
他们真该为自己感到羞愧。

1356
00:58:52.200 --> 00:58:53.200
What a waste.
真是浪费。

1357
00:58:53.200 --> 00:58:55.380
They're here for the dog society.
他们是为了狗狗协会来的。

1358
00:58:55.380 --> 00:58:56.460
And that's what's important.
而那才是最重要的。

1359
00:58:56.800 --> 00:58:58.340
That is his donation.
那是他的捐款。

1360
00:58:58.640 --> 00:58:59.060
Good night.
晚安。

1361
00:58:59.300 --> 00:59:00.780
And he runs out of the room.
然后他跑出了房间。

1362
00:59:01.000 --> 00:59:02.920
Do you think he ever paid the money?
你觉得他付钱了吗？

1363
00:59:03.220 --> 00:59:03.560
No.
没有。

1364
00:59:03.840 --> 00:59:04.460
You don't think?
你不觉得吗？

1365
00:59:04.640 --> 00:59:05.400
I don't think.
我不觉得。

1366
00:59:05.560 --> 00:59:07.780
I think the whole event was like a debacle.
我觉得整个活动就像一场惨败。

1367
00:59:08.200 --> 00:59:12.880
As the evening starts to wrap up, Oscar's going to say good night to the senator.
当晚会接近尾声时，奥斯卡去跟参议员道晚安。

1368
00:59:13.480 --> 00:59:15.540
And the senator says, don't forget to call.
参议员说，别忘了打电话。

1369
00:59:15.700 --> 00:59:19.360
And then he lets his hand linger down Oscar's arm.
然后他的手在奥斯卡的胳膊上停留了一下。

1370
00:59:19.360 --> 00:59:22.920
He brings his hand from the shoulder to the wriSt.
他把手从肩膀滑到了手腕。

1371
00:59:23.400 --> 00:59:26.060
With a series of little squeezes.
还带了一连串的小捏弄。

1372
00:59:27.240 --> 00:59:28.120
Suggestive squeezes.
带有暗示意味的捏弄。

1373
00:59:28.680 --> 00:59:30.040
That was all scripted.
那都是写好的剧本。

1374
00:59:30.280 --> 00:59:32.900
That he would run his hand down Oscar's arm.
他会把手滑过奥斯卡的胳膊。

1375
00:59:33.420 --> 00:59:36.700
Well, Oscar has a talking head where he's like, I still got it.
嗯，奥斯卡有个采访镜头，他说，我宝刀未老。

1376
00:59:36.940 --> 00:59:37.380
Basically.
基本上是这样。

1377
00:59:37.640 --> 00:59:39.060
And oh my God, I feel so bad for Angela.
天哪，我真为安吉拉感到难过。

1378
00:59:39.440 --> 00:59:40.420
Why does this always...
为什么总是……

1379
00:59:43.460 --> 00:59:46.820
And he's now learning to put a diaper on one of the new dogs.
他现在正在学着给其中一只新来的狗换尿布。

1380
00:59:47.660 --> 00:59:50.920
And that's when Jim and Pam and Kevin and Aaron come in to check on him.
就在这时，吉姆、帕姆、凯文和亚伦进来查看他的情况。

1381
00:59:50.920 --> 00:59:52.400
And he's like, I'm doing great.
他说，我做得很好。

1382
00:59:52.780 --> 00:59:53.200
I'm doing great.
我做得很好。

1383
00:59:53.620 --> 00:59:55.700
We got a fan mail flurry about this scene.
我们收到了关于这一幕的粉丝来信狂潮。

1384
00:59:56.080 --> 00:59:59.980
Ainsley said it was maybe our biggest fan mail flurry yet.
安斯利说这可能是我们迄今为止收到过最大规模的粉丝来信。

1385
01:00:00.300 --> 01:00:01.160
You're kidding.
你开玩笑吧。

1386
01:00:01.360 --> 01:00:02.120
The whole time?
一直都是吗？

1387
01:00:02.380 --> 01:00:04.840
The biggest of the whole series that we've been rewatching.
是我们重温整个系列以来规模最大的一次。

1388
01:00:04.840 --> 01:00:06.300
Please tell me what it was.
快告诉我内容是什么。

1389
01:00:06.740 --> 01:00:15.800
At the end of the fundraiser, when we see all the dogs that Andy has adopted, you can see Andy and April's three-legged dog champion from Parks and Rec.
在募捐活动结束时，当我们看到安迪领养的所有狗时，你可以看到安迪和艾普尔在《公园与游憩》里的那只三条腿的冠军狗。

1390
01:00:15.800 --> 01:00:17.220
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1391
01:00:17.600 --> 01:00:17.900
Yeah.
是的。

1392
01:00:18.360 --> 01:00:24.080
So people noticed that we used the same dog as champion in Parks and Rec.
所以人们注意到我们在《公园与游憩》里用了同一只狗，也就是冠军。

1393
01:00:25.420 --> 01:00:27.380
Famous dog spotting, basically.
基本上就是发现了明星狗。

1394
01:00:27.680 --> 01:00:28.340
Fan mail flurry.
粉丝来信狂潮。

1395
01:00:29.260 --> 01:00:32.840
Kevin is going to try to be the voice of reason again in this scene.
凯文在这一幕里又要尝试充当理性的声音了。

1396
01:00:33.020 --> 01:00:33.260
Yeah.
是的。

1397
01:00:33.620 --> 01:00:35.020
And no one's really listening.
但其实没人听他的。

1398
01:00:35.420 --> 01:00:39.620
Kevin has a talking head where he says, sometimes he thinks the people he works with are idiots.
凯文有个采访镜头，他说，有时候他觉得跟他一起工作的人都是白痴。

1399
01:00:39.960 --> 01:00:41.700
Sometimes, meaning all times.
有时候，意思是所有时候。

1400
01:00:42.000 --> 01:00:43.000
All the times.
一直都是。

1401
01:00:43.340 --> 01:00:44.500
Every of the time.
一直都是这样。

1402
01:00:44.960 --> 01:00:45.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1403
01:00:45.800 --> 01:00:54.520
In our tag for this episode, we're going to learn that the dogs have been, I guess, divided up between different folks at Dunder Mifflin.
在本集的标签中，我们将了解到这些狗已经被分给了邓德·米夫林公司的不同员工。

1404
01:00:54.640 --> 01:00:55.500
Daryl has Pepper.
达里尔养了佩珀。

1405
01:00:55.920 --> 01:00:57.100
Kevin has Ruby.
凯文养了鲁比。

1406
01:00:57.920 --> 01:01:00.500
So Aaron and Andy didn't end up with all 12 dogs.
所以亚伦和安迪并没有包揽全部12只狗。

1407
01:01:00.660 --> 01:01:02.240
But they probably have a couple.
但他们可能养了几只。

1408
01:01:02.440 --> 01:01:03.940
They have more than one, for sure.
他们肯定不止养了一只。

1409
01:01:04.060 --> 01:01:05.440
Because you know Angela didn't take one.
因为你知道安吉拉一只都没要。

1410
01:01:05.580 --> 01:01:07.980
Well, Pam and Jim didn't clearly take one.
嗯，帕姆和吉姆显然也没要。

1411
01:01:08.320 --> 01:01:10.740
We learned the most about Kevin's dog, Ruby.
我们对凯文的狗鲁比了解得最多。

1412
01:01:10.960 --> 01:01:12.160
He says she's a good girl.
他说她是个乖女孩。

1413
01:01:12.300 --> 01:01:13.500
She doesn't eat or poop.
她不吃也不拉。

1414
01:01:13.660 --> 01:01:14.820
She just lays there.
她就只是躺在那儿。

1415
01:01:14.820 --> 01:01:19.560
It's very clear that everyone thinks maybe she's dead.
很明显大家都觉得她可能已经死了。

1416
01:01:20.180 --> 01:01:20.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1417
01:01:20.680 --> 01:01:24.100
I mean, he says she smells really bad.
我是说，他说她闻起来很臭。

1418
01:01:24.100 --> 01:01:27.000
But he's afraid that if he puts her in a bath, she'll drown.
但他担心如果给她洗澡，她会淹死。

1419
01:01:27.000 --> 01:01:31.100
Because, you know, even to watch TV, he has to prop her eyes open.
因为，你知道，连看电视时他都得撑开她的眼睛。

1420
01:01:31.440 --> 01:01:34.720
And then there's a very cute scene with Kevin and Ruby.
然后还有一段凯文和鲁比的温馨场景。

1421
01:01:34.720 --> 01:01:36.080
They're laying on the floor together.
他们一起躺在地板上。

1422
01:01:36.080 --> 01:01:40.760
He tells her that everyone is so interested in her and they must be jealous.
他告诉她大家都对她很感兴趣，他们一定很嫉妒。

1423
01:01:40.760 --> 01:01:42.540
And she just starts licking him.
然后她就开始舔他。

1424
01:01:42.660 --> 01:01:43.600
And it's so cute.
那真是太可爱了。

1425
01:01:43.820 --> 01:01:45.240
And she's not dead.
而且她没死。

1426
01:01:45.420 --> 01:01:46.200
She's not dead.
她没死。

1427
01:01:46.200 --> 01:01:48.920
She just likes to nap and doesn't like to bathe.
她只是喜欢打盹，不喜欢洗澡。

1428
01:01:49.260 --> 01:01:50.420
Or eat or poop.
也不喜欢吃东西或排泄。

1429
01:01:50.620 --> 01:01:50.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1430
01:01:50.960 --> 01:01:53.500
We had a fan question from Brendan W.
我们收到了一位粉丝布兰登·W的问题。

1431
01:01:53.680 --> 01:01:58.180
In Indianapolis, Indiana, who said, regarding the ending scene about Kevin's dog, Ruby,
来自印第安纳州印第安纳波利斯的他问到，关于凯文的狗鲁比的结尾场景，

1432
01:01:58.740 --> 01:02:02.240
we're led to believe that his dog is dead, but he just doesn't realize it.
我们被引导认为他的狗已经死了，只是他自己没意识到。

1433
01:02:02.380 --> 01:02:06.860
Was it originally intended to end that way, where Ruby is truly dead?
原本的剧本就是打算以鲁比真的死了来结尾吗？

1434
01:02:07.060 --> 01:02:10.600
Or was it always the writer's intent for the dog to actually be alive?
还是编剧一直都打算让这只狗活着？

1435
01:02:10.600 --> 01:02:15.080
Well, Brendan, it was always the intent that she was actually alive.
嗯，布兰登，编剧一直都打算让她活着。

1436
01:02:15.620 --> 01:02:23.420
I did wonder myself in that final scene with Kevin, if maybe the dog started licking his face,
在凯文的那个最终场景里，我自己在想，如果那只狗开始舔他的脸，

1437
01:02:23.640 --> 01:02:28.040
like, and we kept it, but it was supposed to end with him just talking to this comatose dog.
我们保留了那个镜头，但原本的结尾应该是他对着一只昏迷的狗说话。

1438
01:02:28.320 --> 01:02:28.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1439
01:02:28.920 --> 01:02:32.400
But no, that was a whole little trick that they taught the dog,
但不是的，那是他们教给狗的一个小把戏，

1440
01:02:32.580 --> 01:02:34.680
to kiss his face on that certain word.
在特定的词语出现时去亲吻他的脸。

1441
01:02:34.680 --> 01:02:35.520
Isn't that amazing?
这不是很神奇吗？

1442
01:02:35.840 --> 01:02:36.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1443
01:02:36.380 --> 01:02:36.920
I know.
我知道。

1444
01:02:37.260 --> 01:02:39.280
So, yeah, scripted and achieved.
所以，没错，这是剧本设定并最终实现的。

1445
01:02:39.280 --> 01:02:40.760
Dog actors.
狗狗演员们。

1446
01:02:41.160 --> 01:02:43.100
They're very important to a scene.
它们对一场戏非常重要。

1447
01:02:43.320 --> 01:02:43.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1448
01:02:44.100 --> 01:02:45.140
Well, there you have it, folks.
好了，各位，就是这样。

1449
01:02:45.280 --> 01:02:46.080
That's Fundraiser.
这就是《筹款活动》这一集。

1450
01:02:46.360 --> 01:02:49.820
Thank you so much for listening and sending in your questions and comments.
非常感谢大家的收听以及发来的问题和评论。

1451
